### Page 1 of 3

```text
RESOLUTION NO.________

ENTITLED:  "A RESOLUTION TO ADOPT THE CERTIFICATE OF CANVASS AND
DECLARATION OF RESULTS OF THE CANVASSING BOARD FOR THE
CHEYENNE DOWNTOWN DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY DISTRICT
SPECIAL ELECTION HELD ON OCTOBER 18, 2023."

WHEREAS, a special election of qualified property owners of real property within the
boundaries of the Cheyenne Downtown Development Authority District, excluding real property
used exclusively for residential purposes, was duly called and held on October 18, 2023; and

WHEREAS, a majority of qualified electors cast their vote in favor of the proposal to
authorize a special assessment of twenty (20) mills to be levied upon the assessed value of real
property within the boundaries of the Cheyenne Downtown Development Authority District,
excluding real property used exclusively for residential purposes, which assessment shall be levied
for a period of four (4) years pursuant to Wyoming Statue §15-9-217(b).

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the special election held October 18, 2023, is hereby declared
and ratified to have been duly called, ordered and held in compliance with law;

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that with the approval of the governing body and a
majority of votes cast at the special election on the ballot question submitted to qualified electors
the special assessment of twenty (20) mills was authorized to be levied upon the assessed value of
real property within the established boundaries of the Cheyenne Downtown Development
Authority District of Cheyenne, Wyoming, excluding real property used exclusively for residential
purposes, which assessment shall be levied for a period of four (4) years beginning
January 1, 2024, pursuant to Wyoming Statute § 15-9-217 (b); and

BE IT FINALLY RESOLVED that the Certificate of Canvass and Declaration of Results,
attached to this resolution as Exhibit A, is hereby adopted.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED this _______ day of _____________________,
2023.

__________________________________________
Patrick Collins, Mayor

(SEAL)

ATTEST:

____________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
12:11 pm, Oct 19, 2023
```

